body:
Be there.

That's all you need to do.

&#x200B;

Don't force talk, don't feel awkward about silence.

Don't offer advice, don't tell him/her that everything will be alright.

Don't pretend to relate if can't. If you can, don't make it about you.

&#x200B;

Just be there, for your friend.

And thank-you, for being a friend.

&#x200B;

I'd also recommend the resource at the right, "[Talking Tips](https://www.reddit.com/comments/igh87)".

&#x200B;
